WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.972
The interaction subsystems turn input into navigation, picking,

00:00:07.072 --> 00:00:10.430
selection, measurement, and data scaling, on top of

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.940
the renderer and the compute kernels.

00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:18.458
Three navigation modes share one NavigationControls

00:00:18.558 --> 00:00:20.846
class: orbit, trackball, and fly.

00:00:21.266 --> 00:00:24.912
Orbit circles a target using azimuth and polar angles,

00:00:25.012 --> 00:00:28.797
trackball rotates freely about the target, and fly moves

00:00:28.897 --> 00:00:31.918
the camera itself with keys and pointer look.

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:36.566
Damping smooths motion independently of the frame rate, and fitting

00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:40.510
and inspection views frame your data with smooth transitions.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:44.311
Axis conventions choose which way is up, y, z,

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:48.698
or x, always right-handed, and saved states, pointer lock,

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:51.798
and change events round out the controls.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.569
Picking renders an identifier pass, where every pixel

00:00:57.669 --> 00:01:00.640
stores an object ID and an element index.

00:01:01.066 --> 00:01:05.207
A point pick reads one pixel; rectangle and lasso picks read

00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:09.094
a region and return unique hits, up to a maximum count.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.448
Every object family is pickable, and meshes report triangle

00:01:13.548 --> 00:01:17.634
indices when the device supports the primitive-index feature.

00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:21.587
Each hit carries a world position reconstructed from

00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:25.138
depth, an n-dimensional index for gridded data, and

00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:27.993
attributes when CPU records are retained.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.057
Pick requests are serialized, and picking

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.017
never uses the render-only occlusion filter.

00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:40.654
A selection store keeps hits keyed by object ID and element index.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:44.923
Add, remove, toggle, and replace edit it directly, and

00:01:45.023 --> 00:01:48.220
apply chooses one of those modes at run time.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:53.505
The annotation toolkit builds measurements on top of

00:01:53.605 --> 00:01:56.710
picking, with marker, distance, and angle modes.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:00.360
Distances join two picked anchors, and angles measure

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.494
the corner at the middle of three.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.543
Units set the symbol, decimals, and degrees or radians, while hover

00:02:07.643 --> 00:02:12.357
and selection probes report what the pointer hovers over or selects.

00:02:12.766 --> 00:02:16.389
Records live in the toolkit's own annotation store, not in

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:19.728
the scene, and labels are drawn through the overlay.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.692
A revision counter and change events keep

00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:24.897
interfaces in sync with the store.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.650
The scaling service maps data values into

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.673
the zero-to-one range that colormaps read.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.749
A transform is linear, logarithmic, or symmetric logarithmic, with

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:42.066
optional range or percentile clamping, gamma, and inversion.

00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:46.570
Statistics come from requestStats, which runs on the GPU:

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.699
extract finite values, compact them, find the range, and

00:02:50.799 --> 00:02:54.313
build a histogram when percentiles are requested.

00:02:54.733 --> 00:02:59.668
Percentiles default to two and ninety-eight, estimated from a

00:02:59.768 --> 00:03:04.702
2048-bin histogram, and results are cached until invalidated.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:08.378
Objects apply the results to their own transforms,

00:03:08.478 --> 00:03:10.921
and legends read the same scale state.

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:17.016
To recap: three navigation modes, identifier-pass picking, a

00:03:17.116 --> 00:03:22.013
selection store, measurement annotations, and GPU-backed data scaling.

00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:27.834
The full reference is in the Interaction section of the documentation.
